    "notes": {
        "3c6d9eb5-4f7a-4082-9138-8e4c0d7f2a63": {
            "content": "ENVIRONMENT — this flow is built for:\n- Telegram account: an apiKey account holding a bot token (service appmixer:telegram).\n- Chat: group chat id -5393771328. The bot MUST already be a member of that group.\n- Retargeting: the chat id is a literal on every Telegram component in this flow — change all of them together, or the cleanup step will target a different chat than the one under test.\n\nMANUAL STEP REQUIRED — this flow cannot complete unattended.\nTelegram never delivers a bot its own messages, so the trigger has to be provoked by a human:\n1. Start the flow. The bot posts \"E2E: reply to THIS message...\" into the group.\n2. REPLY to that message in Telegram. A plain new message is not enough — with the bot's privacy mode on it only receives replies to itself and messages that @-mention it.\n3. The trigger fires and the flow deletes the reply. AfterAll waits 600s; with no reply the flow just times out.",
            "x": 64,
            "y": 64,
            "width": 520,
            "height": 300
        }
    }
